.TH head 1 "FUZIX System Utilities" "FUZIX"
.SH NAME
head \- print the first lines of a file
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B head
[\fB\-\fIn\fR] [\fIfile\fR ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B head
prints the first
.I n
lines of each
.IR file ,
ten by default.  With no
.IR file ,
it reads standard input.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \- n
Print
.I n
lines instead of ten.  Only the old form works:
.B head \-20
and not
.BR "head \-n 20" .
The count must be the first argument.
.SH NOTES
No header line is printed between files, even when several are named.
.PP
There is no
.B \-c
byte count.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tail (1),
.BR more (1),
.BR cat (1)
